---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Pro Kit Live Vault | 2026 Relocation & Tax Blueprint">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <!-- VIP Header -->
    <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-indigo-900 via-blue-900 to-slate-900 rounded-3xl p-8 sm:p-10 text-white shadow-xl mb-12 border border-white/10">
      <div class="flex items-center space-x-2 mb-3">
        <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-300 border border-emerald-500/30 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">
          ✓ Verified Member Access
        </span>
        <span class="text-xs text-slate-300">Edition 2026.3 • Synced Weekly</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black tracking-tight">
        Nomad Matrix Pro: Complete Relocation & Tax Blueprint
      </h1>
      <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
        Welcome to your live member vault. This document is dynamically updated as embassies and finance ministries revise visa requirements and tax treaties.
      </p>
      
      <div class="mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-white/10 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 text-xs text-slate-300">
        <div class="flex items-center space-x-2">
          <span class="text-emerald-400">●</span>
          <span>Live Document Status: <strong>Active & Verified</strong></span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center space-x-2">
          <span class="text-blue-400">●</span>
          <span>Coverage: <strong>47 Jurisdictions</strong></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Main Live Content -->
    <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 p-8 sm:p-12 shadow-sm space-y-12">
      <!-- Part 1 -->
      <section>
        <div class="flex items-center space-x-3 mb-4">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 font-bold flex items-center justify-center text-sm">1</span>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Official Visa Document Dossier & Hague Apostille Process</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
          Over 78% of digital nomad visa rejections or administrative delays stem from improper legalizations rather than income shortfalls. Assemble your folder strictly in this order:
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-4 text-sm">
          <div class="p-4 bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/80">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span>📜</span> Police Clearance / Criminal Background Record
            </h3>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 space-y-1 text-slate-600 pl-2">
              <li><strong>Validity Window:</strong> Must be issued within 90 days of your consular interview or online submission.</li>
              <li><strong>Hague Apostille:</strong> If your country is signatory to the 1961 Hague Apostille Convention, it must receive the apostille certificate before translation. Non-Hague countries require full embassy legalization.</li>
              <li><strong>Certified Sworn Translation:</strong> Translations must be done by an accredited court-certified translator (e.g., <em>Traductor Jurado</em> for Spain; certified sworn court translator for Portugal/Italy). Regular agency translations will be rejected.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/80">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span>💼</span> Proof of Remote Work & Contract Seniority
            </h3>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 space-y-1 text-slate-600 pl-2">
              <li><strong>3+ Months Seniority:</strong> Consulates require proof that your employment or freelance contracts have been active for at least 3 months prior to applying.</li>
              <li><strong>Certificate of Good Standing:</strong> Submit an official commercial registry extract proving your foreign employer or main client has been legally incorporated for over 1 year.</li>
              <li><strong>Bank Pay Slips:</strong> 3 to 6 months of consecutive payslips with matched incoming bank transaction references.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/80">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span>🛡️</span> Certified Medical Health Insurance Policy
            </h3>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 space-y-1 text-slate-600 pl-2">
              <li><strong>Zero Deductible ($0 Copay):</strong> Most European consulates mandate zero deductible clauses. Standard credit-card travel insurance with $250-$500 copays is routinely rejected.</li>
              <li><strong>Emergency & Repatriation:</strong> Minimum coverage of €30,000 across the Schengen Area, with explicit repatriation of remains coverage written on the certificate.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Part 2 -->
      <section>
        <div class="flex items-center space-x-3 mb-4">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 font-bold flex items-center justify-center text-sm">2</span>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Employer Remote Work Authorization Template</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          If you work as a full-time or part-time employee, your company must supply an explicit telework authorization letter. Copy and adapt the legally verified wording below onto company letterhead:
        </p>

        <div class="p-6 bg-slate-900 rounded-2xl text-slate-200 text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono leading-relaxed relative">
          <p class="font-bold text-amber-400 mb-4">// COPYABLE EMPLOYER AUTHORIZATION LETTER</p>
          <p>To: The Relevant Consular / Immigration Authority</p>
          <p>Date: [DD/MM/YYYY]</p>
          <br />
          <p>Subject: Official Employer Authorization for Location-Independent Remote Telework</p>
          <br />
          <p>Dear Immigration Officer,</p>
          <br />
          <p>We hereby confirm that <strong>[Employee Full Legal Name]</strong>, holder of passport number <strong>[Passport Number]</strong>, is currently employed on a permanent, continuous basis by <strong>[Legal Entity Name]</strong> (Registration No: [Company Reg Number]) in the capacity of <strong>[Job Title]</strong>, since [Start Date].</p>
          <br />
          <p>We explicitly authorize and support <strong>[Employee Full Legal Name]</strong> to perform 100% of their employment responsibilities remotely from abroad, including while temporarily residing in <strong>[Target Destination Country]</strong>. Their day-to-day work is conducted entirely via telecommunication tools, internet infrastructure, and cloud systems.</p>
          <br />
          <p>Their current gross compensation is <strong>[Monthly Salary Amount & Currency]</strong> (equivalent to approximately $[USD Equivalent] USD per month). This position does not require physical attendance in our offices, and their employment agreement, salary disbursements, and benefits will continue uninterrupted throughout their stay.</p>
          <br />
          <p>Should you require any further documentation or direct corporate verification, please contact the undersigned directly.</p>
          <br />
          <p>Sincerely,</p>
          <p><strong>[Signatory Full Name]</strong></p>
          <p><strong>[Corporate Title, e.g. Chief People Officer / Managing Director]</strong></p>
          <p>[Company Legal Name & Corporate Seal]</p>
          <p>[Corporate Email & Direct Telephone Number]</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Part 3 -->
      <section>
        <div class="flex items-center space-x-3 mb-4">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 font-bold flex items-center justify-center text-sm">3</span>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">2026 Cross-Border Tax Strategies & The 183-Day Rule</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
          Relocating on a digital nomad visa does not automatically make you tax-exempt, but structuring your movements properly can eliminate double taxation legally:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-sm">
          <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-5 bg-slate-50/50">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">1. The 183-Day Physical Presence Trigger</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-600 text-xs leading-relaxed">
              In almost all jurisdictions (including Spain, Portugal, Italy, Japan, and Greece), staying 183 or more days in a calendar year triggers worldwide personal tax residency. To remain non-tax resident, track your border entry/exit stamps and split stays across territorial tax hubs.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-5 bg-slate-50/50">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">2. Territorial Tax Havens for Remote Work</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-600 text-xs leading-relaxed">
              Countries like <strong>Costa Rica, Panama, Georgia, Malaysia, and Albania</strong> operate strict territorial tax regimes: money earned from foreign clients outside their geographic territory incurs 0% local income tax, even if you reside there for months.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-5 bg-slate-50/50">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">3. Spain's Beckham Law for Digital Nomads</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-600 text-xs leading-relaxed">
              Under Spain's Startup Act, Digital Nomad Visa holders can elect into the Non-Resident Income Tax regime (Beckham Law): pay a flat <strong>24%</strong> on Spanish-derived income up to €600,000, with <strong>0% tax on foreign investments, dividends, and capital gains</strong> for 5 years.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-5 bg-slate-50/50">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">4. Bilateral Double Tax Treaties (DTT)</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-600 text-xs leading-relaxed">
              Always request a <em>Certificate of Fiscal Residence</em> from your home tax authority. If both countries hold an active Double Taxation Agreement, you can offset or deduct taxes paid abroad to avoid paying twice on the same invoice.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Part 4: Dynamic Updates Feed -->
      <section class="border-t border-slate-200 pt-10">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Recent Policy Sync Log (2026)</h2>
          <span class="text-xs text-emerald-600 font-semibold bg-emerald-50 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full">Automated Registry Watchdog</span>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-3 text-xs text-slate-600">
          <div class="p-3 bg-slate-50 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-between">
            <span><strong>Italy:</strong> Official Visto Nomadi Digitali operational decree confirmed with €28k threshold.</span>
            <span class="text-slate-400">Synced</span>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3 bg-slate-50 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-between">
            <span><strong>Thailand:</strong> DTV Visa 5-year multi-entry program widely recognized; 180-day stay extensions verified.</span>
            <span class="text-slate-400">Synced</span>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3 bg-slate-50 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-between">
            <span><strong>Spain:</strong> Minimum income calibrated to 200% SMI (~€2,646/mo base for single applicant).</span>
            <span class="text-slate-400">Synced</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <!-- Live Vault Footer Support -->
    <div class="text-center text-xs text-slate-400 mt-10">
      <p>Need custom case evaluation or found a newly issued consulate circular?</p>
      <p class="mt-1 font-medium text-slate-500">Contact the editorial desk: support@apexcraftweb.com</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
